  "body": "It was removed from the W3C fork by @chaals in https://github.com/w3c/html/pull/144 with rather little detail.\n\n@Hixie added this in b50ed926759f4058464e0fd0d32831584c0b693d with this email to the list:\nhttps://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-whatwg-archive/2009May/0014.html\n\nHere's a test that enumerates the properties of HTMLElement.prototype:\nhttp://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=3972\n\nIt looks like only Gecko has implemented `accessKeyLabel`, tracked by this bug:\nhttps://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=583533\n\nI see @dzbarsky, @smaug----, @mstange, @mounirlamouri, @sicking and @bzbarsky on that bug. Do any of you know if this is an awesome feature or a failed experiment that it's time to end?\n",
